Greetings,

I wanted to touch base with you all as we work to strengthen BFD's Public E=
ducation program, focusing in on our 2017 goals and the process for handlin=
g all Pub Ed requests.

Goals:

*         Get to "YES" if at all possible (fulfill as many Pub Ed requests =
as possible)

*         Maintain our annual presence in schools

*         Provide off-duty Pub Ed group support to assigned on-duty crews f=
or complex or lengthy (over 1 hour) events

*         Focus curriculum on high-risk populations/high-hazard occupancies=
 (kids, seniors; residential, institutional)

*         Deliver 3-4 free CPR/AED training events to public during 2017

*         Greater use of the fire safety house; train Pub Ed group members =
on its use

*         Deliver a weekly social media message via Facebook/Twitter

*         Improve tracking/documentation of Pub Ed events

*         Clarify the process for assigning crews and staff to Pub Ed event=
s

Assignment Process:

*         Dana Whitfield will take the lead in receiving and processing r=
equests

*         All requests submitted via online form at https://www.example.org/ser=
vices/education/presentations-tours/pages/fire-tours.aspx (this helps is as=
signing, tracking events, and gathering metrics)

*         Assignments will be made using the following criteria:

*         Station tour requests, non-specialized presentations < 1 hour, an=
d other requests < 1 hour (i.e. visit to pre-school):  on-duty crew

*         Requests greater than 1 hour (i.e. safety fair):  on-duty crew(s)=
 + Pub Ed group member(s)

*         Specialized presentations (career fairs, CPR, evacuation vs. Shel=
ter-in-Place, fire safety house demo):  Pub Ed group member(s)

*         For station tours and other requests < 1 hour, Dana will assign =
directly to a duty crew after reviewing the BFD activity calendar

*         For requests > 1 hour, Dana will email shift BC (with a copy to =
BC Henkel) for crew assignment

*         For requests meeting criteria for Pub Ed group members, Dana wil=
l email DC Ellery

*         Captain VanderMey (Pub Ed group leader) will coordinate Pub Ed gr=
oup assignments

*         BCs/DC must email Dana the assigned on-duty crew/Pub Ed group me=
mbers

*         BCs continue to consider rotating on-duty crews in/out to support=
 lengthy requests (i.e. a 5-hour safety fair)

*         The assigned lead (typically a company officer or Pub Ed group me=
mber) will receive an automated "You've been assigned..." email with the de=
tails of the event

Closing the loop (company officer or Pub Ed group member):

*         Upon completing the event (preferably the same day), the assigned=
 lead closes out the event in Staff Central "Fire Tours"

*         click on your event

*         click on "Edit Item"

*         enter the amount of time, number of attendees, topics covered, et=
c at the bottom of the form

*         click "Save"

If you have any questions or concerns, please send them my way.

Pat Ellery
Division Chief - Life Safety Division
Bellingham Fire Department
(555) 010-8422
pellery@example.org

My incoming and outgoing email messages are subject to public disclosure re=
quirements per RCW 42.56



